      },
      "message": "feat(wire): control and wear wire offset for Wire Contour (COMP records)\n\nA Wire Contour states a compensation mode: computer (the default),\ncontrol or wear. The generator still makes and judges the wire-centre\npath. With control or wear, each pass gets one CompSpan\n(wire_edm::wire_comp_spans): the part contour (control) or the\nwire-centre walk (wear), with the pass's kerf offset as its radius. The\ndump writes it between COMP records, so the Sodick LN2W post writes\nG41/G42 Hnnn by pass and G40 on each lead-out.\n\n- door and generation refuse an open run, a 4-axis cut, a taper, a\n  burnout, tabs, the arc lead and an exit pick by name\n- the DTO key `compensation` is written only when not computer; the\n  stamp digests it only then; MCP lists it and the skill row names it\n- new LN2W goldens: edm_test_square_offset.nc, edm_test_2axis_offset.nc\n\nFixes #4134\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
